invariant: INV-16
file: src/p256_wide_field.h
catches: p256_equiv_test
reason: p256_wide_fe_reduce_once subtracts p from the four low words alone
  and takes its mask from their borrow, so a sum that carried past 2^256
  keeps its four low words where it needs p taken off. Such a sum then
  leaves the field 2^256 - p too small. bin/p256_equiv_test compares every
  wide field routine with p256_field.c's on the same words, edge values
  that carry among them.

--- old
    (void)p256_wide_sub_borrow(&borrow, high, 0);
    uint64_t keep = p256_wide_mask(borrow);
--- new
    (void)high;
    uint64_t keep = p256_wide_mask(borrow);
